  },
  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce ground beef",
    "1 large egg",
    "1/4 cup parmesan cheese (grated)",
    "1/2 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1 1/2 cup water",
    "1/4 cup apple cider vinegar",
    "3 tablespoon soy sauce (or coconut aminos)",
    "1/3 cup low-carb ketchup",
    "1 cup erythritol",
    "1/2 teaspoon xanthan gum"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "In a large mixing bowl, combine the ground beef, egg, parmesan, and onion powder. Mix together by hand.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use a tablespoon to measure out and shape the meatballs.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat a saucepan over medium heat. Add the meatballs and cook until browned on the outside (if they're still slightly pink in the middle, that's okay for now). Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the same saucepan, add the water, apple cider vinegar, soy sauce, sugar-free ketchup, and erythritol. Whisk until the sauce comes together. Slowly whisk in the xanthan gum. Add only a little at a time, waiting a couple minutes in between to make sure it thickens first. Lower the temperature and let the sauce simmer on low.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a couple of minutes, check the sauce for the desired consistency. Run a spoon through the sauce to see whether it coats the back — a properly thickened sauce will not immediately run back together. Add the meatballs and let simmer on low for 10 minutes or until the meatballs are cooked through.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve and enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs/#wprm-recipe-52131-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2017/04/low-carb-sweet-and-sour-meatballs-step-06.jpg"
    }
  ],
